# Section children are articles

Every first-level child of a `<section>` is an `<article>`. Do not mount a page-level card as a `div`.

All articles share one look: the project's page-level surface chrome plus the full width of the page measure — wide content, same theming. The project's card component composes that level, so a card is an `<article>`.

Nested chrome (tile, floating, menu, control, pill, table) stays a `div`.

Instantiation: point the `globs` above at this project's component file
extension and name the project's own surface/card classes in place of this
generic wording ([[CLONE]]). A headless project deletes this rule.
